Title: LAST FLIGHT OF THE OSPREY
Credit: written by
Author: Storyboard AI Standard Benchmark
Notes: 5-Minute Short Film (5 Scenes, Complete 3-Act Mini-Arc)

EXT. MOJAVE DESERT AIRSTRIP - DUSK
[SCENE 1 - ACT I: THE CHALLENGE]
The sun sinks behind burnt red mountains. A vintage 1948 crop-duster plane, "The Osprey", sits on cracked asphalt. ELI (60s, weathered bomber jacket, oil-stained hands) tightens the propeller hub.

INT. HANGAR OFFICE - NIGHT
[SCENE 2 - ACT I: THE CALL]
A rotary telephone rings insistently. Eli picks up.
DISPATCHER (O.S.)
Eli, the mountain hospital in Bishop ran out of antivenom. Roads are blocked by a mudslide. You're the only pilot within two hundred miles with night flight clearance.

EXT. AIRSTRIP RUNWAY - NIGHT
[SCENE 3 - ACT II: THE TAKEOFF]
Lightning illuminates towering storm clouds over the Sierra Nevada range. The Osprey's radial engine COUGHS, SPUTTERS, and ROARS to life. Eli accelerates into the black gale.

EXT. SIERRA PEAKS - NIGHT - STORM
[SCENE 4 - ACT II: THE CRISIS]
Violent turbulence tosses the small plane like a leaf. Ice builds up on the canvas wings. The altimeter spins wildly as engine cylinder three MISFIRES. Eli cuts fuel mix and dives into the canyon valley!

EXT. BISHOP COMMUNITY HOSPITAL HELIPAD - DAWN
[SCENE 5 - ACT III: THE RESOLUTION]
The storm breaks into soft morning pinks. The Osprey taxis to a halt beside waiting paramedics. Eli steps down, hands the insulated medicine crate to the lead doctor, and looks back at the rising sun.
